  "description": "Experience the unique and exciting blend of classic main line running and thrilling high-speed commuting, aboard state-of-the-art motive power, in London and the Garden of England with Train Sim World®: Southeastern Highspeed – now including Ashford International and Dartford!\n\nVersatility and modern precision combine in the BR Class 395 EMU, Britain’s fastest train, operating at 140mph to offer commuters domestic high-speed services between London, Ebbsfleet International and Ashford International on the state-of-the-art HS1, as well as being able to operate on Kent’s classic main lines through to Medway and Faversham. Master the TVM430 signalling and power change modes in this sleek masterpiece.\n\nTake charge of classic services on the Chatham Main Line with the reliable BR Class 375/9, running in a variety of formations between Rochester and Faversham. This southern region mainstay has been in service since the turn of the century, continue its next chapter by keeping an eye on the signals and weaving through the Medway Towns.\n\nGet a taste of the 90s with the unmistakable motor whines of the BR Class 465/9, fill in the gaps with additional commuter services on the Chatham Main Line, or go full “Kent Link Networker” on the many trains that stretch between Medway, Gravesend and Dartford. Keep up your precision to stay on schedule."
